<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">11 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 11 November, from 308 to 1965.</p></header>
<div class="tih-pinned-card"><p class="tih-pinned-label">International day</p><p class="tih-pinned-title">Remembrance Day</p><p class="tih-pinned-desc">Observed each year at the eleventh hour of the eleventh day of the eleventh month — the moment the Armistice ending the First World War took effect in 1918 — Remembrance Day honours the sacrifice of military personnel who have died in all wars since.</p></div>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/diocletian" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/diocletian.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">308 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,718 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Diocletian, Galerius and Maximian confer at Carnuntum</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">With the former emperors <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diocletian">Diocletian</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maximian">Maximian</a> present, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galerius">Galerius</a> appointed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/licinius">Licinius</a> as Augustus in place of Severus, killed by Maxentius, and Maximian was ordered to step down for good. The meeting aimed to end the civil wars of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tetrarchy">Tetrarchy</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carnuntum">Carnuntum</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galerius">Galerius</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maximian">Maximian</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1215">1215 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">811 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Innocent III opens the Fourth Lateran Council</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The largest church council of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> met in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> under Innocent III. It defined transubstantiation, required annual confession and ordered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> and Muslims to wear distinguishing dress.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1500">1500 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">526 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Louis XII and Ferdinand II secretly agree to divide Naples</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the secret Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xii-of-france">Louis XII of France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-ii-of-aragon">Ferdinand II of Aragon</a> agreed to partition the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a>. Disputes between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and the Hispanic kingdoms led to the treaty's collapse in 1503.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xii-of-france">Louis XII of France</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-ii-of-aragon">Ferdinand II of Aragon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1778">1778 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">248 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">British and Iroquois forces attack Cherry Valley, New York</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A mixed force of Loyalists, British soldiers, Senecas and Mohawks attacked the fort and town of Cherry Valley in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>, whose defenders were unprepared despite warnings. The attackers killed 14 soldiers and 30 civilians.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American Revolutionary War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1831">1831 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">195 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nat Turner is hanged in Virginia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Nat Turner was executed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>, for leading the August revolt in which about 55 to 60 white people were killed. Reprisals killed many more Black people, and southern states tightened slave codes.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1918">1918 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">108 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The armistice ends fighting on the Western Front</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Signed at 5 a.m. in a railway carriage in the forest of Compiègne, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-11-november-1918">armistice</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> took effect at 11 o'clock. The day is marked as Armistice or Remembrance Day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1921">1921 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">105 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Tomb of the Unknown Soldier is dedicated at Arlington</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President Harding presided as an unidentified American soldier from the Western Front was buried at Arlington National Cemetery. A year earlier, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> had interred their own unknown warriors.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1965">1965 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">61 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rhodesia declares independence from Britain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ian-smith">Ian Smith</a>'s white minority government issued a Unilateral Declaration of Independence to avoid majority rule. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and the UN imposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanctions">sanctions</a>, and after a long <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> war <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwe">Zimbabwe</a> became independent in 1980.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwe">Zimbabwe</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 11 November <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-holy-roman-emperor"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-iv-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Henry IV, Holy Roman Emperor</span><span class="tp">1050–1106</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alphonse-count-of-poitiers"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alphonse-count-of-poitiers.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alphonse, Count of Poitiers</span><span class="tp">1220–1271</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/martin-bucer"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/martin-bucer.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Martin Bucer</span><span class="tp">1491–1551</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/victor-emmanuel-iii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/victor-emmanuel-iii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Victor Emmanuel III</span><span class="tp">1869–1947</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/carlos-fuentes"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/carlos-fuentes.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Carlos Fuentes</span><span class="tp">1928–2012</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/daniel-ortega"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/daniel-ortega.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Daniel Ortega</span><span class="tp">b. 1945</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jigme-singye-wangchuck"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Jigme Singye Wangchuck</span><span class="tp">b. 1955</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 11 November <span class="n">8</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/teutberga"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Teutberga</span><span class="tp">d. 875</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/teresa-countess-of-portugal"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/teresa-countess-of-portugal.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Teresa, Countess of Portugal</span><span class="tp">c. 1080–1130</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/peter-iii-of-aragon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/peter-iii-of-aragon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Peter III of Aragon</span><span class="tp">1239–1285</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/stefan-decanski"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/stefan-decanski.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Stefan Dečanski</span><span class="tp">c. 1285–1331</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gerald-fitzgerald-14th-earl-of-desmond"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Gerald FitzGerald, 14th Earl of Desmond</span><span class="tp">c. 1533–1583</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/soren-kierkegaard"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/soren-kierkegaard.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Søren Kierkegaard</span><span class="tp">1813–1855</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/yasser-arafat"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Yasser Arafat</span><span class="tp">1929–2004</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/f-w-de-klerk"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/f-w-de-klerk.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">F. W. de Klerk</span><span class="tp">1936–2021</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
